@startuml CorrectnessProofSequence
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam sequence {
    ActorBackgroundColor #E8F5E9
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #E3F2FD
    DatabaseBackgroundColor #FFF9C4
}

title Formal Proof of Correctness - Induction on Visited Set |S|\nTheorem: When node u is dequeued, d[u] = delta(s, u)

actor "Mathematical Induction" as Proof

participant "Base Case:\n|S| = 1" as Base
participant "Inductive Hypothesis:\n|S| = k" as IH
participant "Inductive Step:\n|S| = k+1" as IS
participant "Contradiction Proof" as Contradiction

Proof -> Base: **Initialize source s**
activate Base
note right of Base
  - d[s] = 0 (by definition)
  - delta(s,s) = 0 (trivial path)
  - Therefore: d[s] = delta(s,s) [OK]
  - All weights w >= 0, so no negative cycle
end note
Base -> Proof: [OK] Base case holds

Proof -> IH: **Assume for |S| = k**
activate IH
note right of IH
  For all x in S (|S| = k):
  d[x] = delta(s,x)
  
  S contains k finalized nodes
  All have optimal distances
end note
IH -> Proof: [OK] Inductive hypothesis set

Proof -> IS: **Prove for |S| = k+1**
activate IS
note right of IS
  Let u be next node dequeued:
  u = argmin{d[v] : v in PQ}
  
  Claim: d[u] = delta(s,u)
end note

IS -> Contradiction: **Assume d[u] > delta(s,u)**
activate Contradiction
note right of Contradiction
  Let p* be true shortest path s to u
  Since s in S and u not in S, p* crosses
  the boundary of S at some edge (x,y)
  where x in S and y not in S
end note

Contradiction -> IS: **When x was finalized:**
note left of IS
  d[x] = delta(s,x) (by IH)
  Edge (x,y) was relaxed:
  d[y] <= d[x] + w(x,y)
  d[y] <= delta(s,x) + w(x,y)
  d[y] <= delta(s,y) (by Optimal Substructure)
end note

IS -> Contradiction: **Prefix argument:**
note right of Contradiction
  y is prefix of path to u:
  delta(s,y) <= delta(s,u) (remaining weights >= 0)
  
  Therefore: d[y] <= delta(s,u)
end note

Contradiction -> IS: **Heap property:**
note left of IS
  u was dequeued before y:
  d[u] <= d[y] (min-heap)
  
  Combined: d[u] <= d[y] <= delta(s,u)
  But we assumed d[u] > delta(s,u)
  
  CONTRADICTION! QED
end note

IS -> Proof: **Therefore: d[u] = delta(s,u) [OK]**

Proof -> Proof: **Termination:**
note right of Proof
  Each node enters S at most once
  |S| increases by 1 per iteration
  After at most V iterations: terminates
  
  Final state: All reachable nodes
  have d[v] = delta(s,v) [OK]
end note

@enduml
